  "progression": [
    "Year one builds language from Proficiency 1 to 4, with 2 requiring attendance of 1, 3 requiring 1–2 and 4 requiring 1–3. The diagnostic Dutch test and tutoring carry no credits. Contemporary France lists B1.2/B2 reading and listening preparation.",
    "A positive binding study advice is required for the post-first-year components, normally reached at 48 EC. The 30 EC abroad component additionally specifies at least 54 EC in year one and attendance in the first semester of year two. Full normal progression satisfies both. Annex 1 permits a board-approved 30 EC substitute for valid reasons.",
    "Year three contains advanced written French, literary classics, 30 EC approved electives, a research workshop and the 12 EC research project. The project requires the binding study advice, prior disciplinary material and adequate written French. The normal sequence develops this preparation, with the workshop preceding the project."
  ]
